ighten this toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 47 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Greg Landsman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term incumbent Greg Landsman defends a Cincinnati-area seat that was redrawn to lean slightly Republican, facing Republican Eric Conroy and a Libertarian in November. Landsman holds a decisive financial edge, with about $3.6 million on hand to Conroy's $474,000, and has outraised his challenger roughly three to one. Outside spending has been minimal so far.\n\nRaters broadly place the race in the Likely or Lean Democratic column, though two call it Safe D and Inside Elections says Tilt D, reflecting the district's new partisan tilt. The only available poll, from August, showed Landsman up four points among likely voters. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket price his win chances in the high 80s. The combination of incumbency, money, and expert consensus favors Landsman, but the redrawn terrain and sparse polling keep the race from being rated safe.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8833, "margin": 7.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8451, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8473, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8639, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8273, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7978, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.84, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.87, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8688, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8815, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8538, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 7.2}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8433, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.866, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8525, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem